/// What every layer of a target extends, through the trait of its role. A target is an ace const
/// of the project holding the Target of lib/target/main.lfy; each of its layers is applied to
/// that const, so a layer's criteria are guidance the compiler receives with every request, its
/// knowledge is given to the compiler to read, and its commands are listed for it to run. A target
/// is assembled from packages and is never a change to the compiler.
trait target: `A layer of a target: one thing the compiler is told about building for it` {
  $provides: `Capabilities this layer gives its target, such as http-server or node-api` = string[];
  $requires: `Capabilities some layer of its target must provide` = string[];
  $outputExtensions: `Extensions, without the dot, that outputs may have besides the language's own` = string[];
  .provides = [];
  .requires = [];
  .outputExtensions = [];

  // Capabilities
  where (`Several layers of one target set provides, requires, or outputExtensions`) -> `The target has every item any of them set, in the order the layers are applied`;
  where (`A capability a layer of a target requires is provided by no layer of that target`) -> `A problem at the target's const names the target and the capability`;

  // Guidance
  where (`The compiler is handed a request for a batch of units of the target`) -> `It treats each criterion of the guidance as a rule of the target`;
  where (`Two criteria of the guidance conflict, or one is ambiguous for the unit at hand`) -> `The compiler stops on that unit and quotes the criterion; it never guesses`;
  where (`The knowledge a request gives leaves open how something is written`) -> `The compiler asks for clarification rather than guess`;

  // Outputs
  where (`An output is written`) -> `Its path is under the target's output directory; nothing outside that directory is written`;
}
